# References And Data

A `Jido.Flow.Ref` reads data when a Flow executes. References are also the
source of inferred graph dependencies.

Run the cells from top to bottom.

## Install The Package

```elixir
Mix.install([{:jido_action, "~> 3.0.0-beta.1"}])
```

## Define An Action And Flow

```elixir
defmodule FlowReferences.Echo do
  use Jido.Action, name: "flow_references_echo"

  @impl true
  def run(params, _context), do: {:ok, params}
end

defmodule FlowReferences.Example do
  use Jido.Flow, name: "flow_references_example"

  flow do
    step "profile",
      action: FlowReferences.Echo,
      params: %{
        user: input([:request, :user]),
        actor_id: context(:actor_id),
        literal: value("profile")
      }

    step "summary",
      action: FlowReferences.Echo,
      params: %{
        name: result("profile", [:user, :name]),
        actor_id: select(result("profile"), [:actor_id])
      }

    output(%{summary: result("summary")})
  end
end
```

```elixir
{:ok, output} =
  Jido.Exec.run(
    FlowReferences.Example,
    %{request: %{user: %{name: "Ada"}}},
    %{actor_id: "user-1"}
  )

output
```

## Global References

| DSL helper | Canonical source | Reads |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `input(path)` | `:input` | Validated Flow input. |
| `context(path)` | `:context` | Caller context. |
| `result(name, path)` | `:result` | Named component output. |
| `select(ref, path)` | same as source | A deeper path on a reference. |

A path can be one atom, string, non-negative integer, or a list of these
segments. Missing keys and invalid list indexes return structured execution
errors.

A result reference creates an inferred dependency on the named component.
Input and context references do not.

## Local References

Local helpers are valid only in their component scope.

| Scope | Helpers |
| --- | --- |
| Map params | `item`, `item_index`, `item_id` |
| Reduce params | `item`, `item_index`, `item_id`, `accumulator` |
| Iterate params | `state`, `iteration_index` |
| Iterate State update | `state`, `iteration_index`, `body_result` |
| Iterate completion | `state`, `iteration_index` |

The validator rejects a local reference outside its scope. This keeps the data
grammar explicit before execution.

## Portable Literals

Flow literals are `nil`, Boolean values, numbers, strings, and registered
atoms. Lists must be proper lists. Use maps, not keyword lists. Stored JSON
uses a trusted Registry for atoms and atom map keys.
